    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (the other two files are an abstract base and a log-capture helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `ageBand` feature for owner registration. The app generates DTOs from `openapi.yml` and computes derived read-only fields in `OwnerMapper`, so I followed that existing pattern:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (optional ISO date input) to the `OwnerFields` schema, and `ageBand` (read-only enum `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` schema.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` column with getter/setter, mirroring `registrationDate`.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on HSQLDB.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `ageBand` mapping: when `birthDate` is present, it computes the full years between `birthDate` and the stored (defaulted/business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate` via `Period.between`, mapping `<18 \u2192 MINOR`, `18\u201364 \u2192 ADULT`, `65+ \u2192 SENIOR`. Absent when no birth date is set.\n\nThe request's `birthDate` maps automatically into the entity (MapStruct name match), and `ageBand` is derived on read against `registrationDate`. The test (`birthDate=1990-01-01`, registrationDate defaults to today) correctly yields `ADULT`.",
